# ── Generated site data (never hand-edit, never commit) ───────────────────
# Rebuilt from works/ by scripts/lib/build_works_index.py. Every consumer
# regenerates these before use — the Pages deploy (.github/workflows/build.yml)
# and all four process-*.yml automations — so the copies in git were pure
# redundancy and made every corpus PR ambiguous. Recreate locally with
# ./scripts/bootstrap --quick. See "Data tiers" in CLAUDE.md.
docs/data/index.jsonl
docs/data/archive.jsonl
docs/data/songs/
docs/data/tabs/*.otf.json
# ...but NOT the hand-placed OTF test fixtures. These are authored, not
# generated: build_works_index's orphan prune deliberately spares them and
# docs/js/__tests__/otf-editor/facade-27493.test.js reads one directly.
!docs/data/tabs/*_tef.otf.json
# Lowered form of curation/bounty_decisions.yaml (which IS tracked — it's the
# hand-authored source). Rebuilt by scripts/lib/bounty_decisions.py on every
# index build, and its chord counts come from the freshly written index, so a
# committed copy would go stale the moment a work gains chords.
docs/data/bounty_decisions.json
# ...and the board itself, now that build_wanted.py regenerates it during the
# index build. curation/bounty_decisions.yaml and docs/data/bluegrass_catalogue.json
# ARE tracked — they are the hand-authored and locally-produced inputs.
docs/data/wanted_songs.json
